# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit real values.
# Add every new variable here (with a comment) in the same PR that introduces it.

# Alpaca market data (Phase 2 PriceSource). These are the data keys; they are never
# used by the order path.
# ALPACA_API_KEY=
# ALPACA_API_SECRET=
# Alpaca paper trading (Phase 4 Broker adapter): separate paper keys, so a
# live-capable key is never in the order path. The endpoint is paper-only by a
# guarded setting that no environment variable can change (docs/specs/paper-trading.md
# req 2; Phase 6 changes it by ADR).
# These two are book `main`'s pair (H1's book, ADR 0017 B.1).
# ALPACA_PAPER_API_KEY=
# ALPACA_PAPER_API_SECRET=
# Every other paper book has its own Alpaca paper account and its own pair, named by
# its book token upper-cased (plan T153): ALPACA_PAPER_BOOKS__<TOKEN>__API_KEY and
# ALPACA_PAPER_BOOKS__<TOKEN>__API_SECRET. Tokens with a pair are lower-case letters
# and digits; a book with no pair cannot start (`no_credentials`), and a pair that
# repeats the data keys, `main`'s or another book's is refused. Never fall back to
# `main`'s pair. An ALPACA_PAPER_BOOKS__MAIN__* entry is never read. For example,
# for a book `daily`:
# ALPACA_PAPER_BOOKS__DAILY__API_KEY=
# ALPACA_PAPER_BOOKS__DAILY__API_SECRET=
# Set by the launchd plist for the scheduled `paper run` (docs/runbooks/scheduling.md),
# never in .env: marks the run's `invoked_by` as `scheduler` for the exit-criteria count.
# TRADEPARTNER_INVOKED_BY=scheduler
# Optional `email` alert channel (alerts.channels); all four are needed for it to send.
# ALERT_SMTP_HOST=
# ALERT_SMTP_USER=
# ALERT_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# ALERT_EMAIL_TO=
# Optional sender; defaults to ALERT_SMTP_USER. Set it when the login is not a mailbox.
# ALERT_EMAIL_FROM=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# SEC EDGAR requires a declared User-Agent with a name and contact email,
# and rate-limits at ~10 req/s (docs/decisions/0003-data-adapters-local-first.md).
# SEC_EDGAR_USER_AGENT="Your Name your@email"
# Config keys use the nested delimiter `__` and JSON for lists (src/tradepartner/config.py).
# DuckDB caps on every store connection (#1418), an OOM guard for long runs. Unset keeps
# DuckDB's default (80% of RAM, one thread per core). memory_limit is a size with a unit
# (KB/MB/GB/TB or KiB/MiB/GiB/TiB); threads is a positive integer.
# STORE__MEMORY_LIMIT=6GB
# STORE__THREADS=4
# Successor ids the owner accepted that `master-retract` must never propose (#922;
# docs/specs/data-foundation.md, #859 amendment). Default empty. MTCH (#828):
# MASTER__KEEP_SUCCESSORS='["0000891103@2020-08-10"]'
# Strategy lab (docs/specs/strategy-lab.md, T93). `schedule.*` is frozen per hypothesis
# (ADR 0012); `holdout.*` stays absent from this file (no owner default to leak).
# SCHEDULE__REBALANCE_CADENCE=month_end
# SCHEDULE__SIGNAL_ANCHOR=month_end
# `profitability` family (backtest spec amendment #720): frozen per hypothesis;
# list keys take JSON.
# PROFITABILITY__BASIS=gross
# PROFITABILITY__ANNUAL_PERIOD_DAYS='[350, 380]'
# PROFITABILITY__MAX_FACT_AGE_DAYS=548
# PROFITABILITY__EXCLUDE_SIC_RANGES='[[6000, 6999]]'
# PROFITABILITY__INCLUDE_DERIVED=true
# PROFITABILITY__TOP_FRACTION=0.10
# PROFITABILITY__WEIGHTING=equal
# `combined` family (hypothesis backlog B4): the fixed equal-rank combination of
# momentum and profitability; frozen per hypothesis.
# COMBINED__TOP_FRACTION=0.10
# COMBINED__WEIGHTING=equal
# B10's share-turnover screen (backtest spec amendment #1358), a `momentum` rule in
# (0, 1]; 1.0 is no screen. A hypothesis or sweep file names it to use it: a file that
# leaves it out freezes 1.0, never this value, so setting it here changes no
# registration.
# STRATEGY__TURNOVER_TOP_FRACTION=1.0
# `lab.*` sweep and quiet-interval rules; dict and list keys take JSON.
# LAB__SWEEPABLE_KEYS='["strategy.formation_months", "strategy.top_fraction"]'
# LAB__MAX_VARIANTS_PER_SWEEP=100
# LAB__PROMOTION_MIN_DSR_EXCESS=0.5
# LAB__AXIS_LATTICE='{"strategy.top_fraction": 0.01}'
# LAB__QUIET_INTERVALS='[["16:00", "21:00"]]'
# LAB__QUIET_WEEKDAYS='[0, 1, 2, 3, 4]'
# LAB__QUIET_TIMEZONE=America/New_York
# LAB__SECONDS_PER_VARIANT_DEFAULT='{"month_end": 1.0, "week_end": 4.0, "daily": 20.0}'
# Security ids the owner accepted as genuine long-gap relistings: the resolver never
# cuts their spans at a stopped line (#943; docs/specs/data-foundation.md rule 7,
# amendment #943). Default empty. MiMedx:
# ALPACA__ACCEPTED_RELISTINGS='["0001376339"]'
# Research labeling (docs/specs/research-labeling.md reqs 7, 8 and 17; ADR 0013). The
# model client can be built only when BOTH ceilings exceed 0 AND the key is set; the
# defaults (0.0, 0.0, absent) mean no model call is possible (ADR 0013 point 3 (e)).
# The vendor key, read only by src/tradepartner/research/models.py and redacted from
# every stored message; owner-held, never given to an agent.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# Spend ceilings in USD, month-to-date and cumulative, summed from the inference
# records (owner decision 2026-10-06: both 40; ADR 0013's dated section first, T125).
# RESEARCH__SPEND_CEILING_USD_MONTH=0.0
# RESEARCH__SPEND_CEILING_USD_TOTAL=0.0
